IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what a current or former member of
-- the Australian Defence Force meets: whether an injury or disease is a "service injury" or "service disease" (s 27) and
-- the standard of proof (s 335); whether the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Commission must accept liability,
-- and the exclusions (ss 23, 32 to 36); how a claim is made (s 319); permanent impairment compensation -- entitlement, the
-- threshold, when it is payable from, the lump sum choice and when the lump sum is paid (ss 68, 69, 74, 77 to 79);
-- incapacity compensation for a former member -- which weekly rate applies and when it stops (ss 118 to 122, 129, 131);
-- and review by the Veterans' Review Board and the Tribunal (ss 345, 352A, 352B, 354).
--
-- SEAT: the member or former member. "I was injured or became ill in ADF service after 1 July 2004. Is my condition
-- accepted, and what compensation, incapacity payments and permanent impairment payments do I get?" The Commission's
-- determinations and the opinions the Act hands it are encoded conditionally, as what they mean for that person.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 77, compilation date 29 September 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 94, 2026 (register id
-- C2026C00443), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01285.txt.
--
-- FORMULAS LOST IN THE DEPOSIT. The weekly incapacity formulas (ss 129(1), 130(2), (3), 131(1)) and the lump sum formula
-- (s 78(5)) read "the following formula:" with nothing after. The encoding answers which incapacity rate applies and the
-- adjustment percentage, and which lump sum percentages may be chosen, not the dollar amounts. See NOTES.md finding 1.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. A condition from before 1 July 2004 (the Consequential and Transitional Provisions Act, the DRCA and the
-- VEA) answers `not covered`. The Statements of Principles and the s 27A presumptions; s 24 (service death) and Chapter 5
-- (dependants); the Guide to Determining Impairment and Compensation (s 67), so the weekly amount of permanent impairment
-- compensation is not computed; ss 70 to 72, 75, 80 to 83A; Chapter 3 (rehabilitation); incapacity of current members
-- (Part 3 of Chapter 4) and the Special Rate Disability Pension (Part 6); Chapter 6 (treatment); ss 320 to 343 beyond
-- s 319 and s 335; reconsideration (ss 347 to 350) except as a route; the Board's procedure (ss 352C onwards).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 -- the member's questions`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- s 2: ss 3 to 359 commenced on 1 July 2004; which Act governs an earlier injury is settled by the transitional Act
    `a condition sustained or contracted before 1 July 2004 is governed by the transitional provisions, the DRCA or the VEA, which are not encoded`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `ss 6, 27, 335 -- is it a service injury or disease`

-- s 27: "an injury sustained, or a disease contracted, by a person is a service injury or a service disease if one or
-- more of the following apply: (a) the injury or disease resulted from an occurrence that happened while the person was a
-- member rendering defence service; (b) the injury or disease arose out of, or was attributable to, any defence service
-- rendered by the person while a member; (c) in the opinion of the Commission: (i) the injury was sustained due to an
-- accident that would not have occurred; or (ii) the disease would not have been contracted; but for" the defence service
-- or changes in the person's environment because of it; "(d)" a condition sustained during service but not arising out of
-- it, or before a period of service, that "in the opinion of the Commission ... was contributed to in a material degree
-- by, or was aggravated by, any defence service"; "(da) the injury was sustained while the person was on duty as a member,
-- whether or not as a result of performing that duty; (e) the injury or disease resulted from an accident that occurred
-- while the person was travelling, while a member rendering peacetime service but otherwise than in the course of duty, on
-- a journey: (i) to a place for the purpose of performing duty; or (ii) away from a place of duty upon having ceased to
-- perform duty." The Commission's opinions in (c) and (d) are asked as facts.
DECLARE `How it happened` IS ONE OF
    `it resulted from something that happened while I was a member rendering defence service`
    `it arose out of, or is attributable to, my defence service`
    `it would not have happened but for my defence service, or the change in my surroundings it brought, in the Commission's opinion`
    `an existing condition was materially contributed to or aggravated by my later defence service, in the Commission's opinion`
    `I was injured while on duty, whether or not because of the duty`
    `an accident while travelling to duty, or home from duty, in peacetime service`
    `none of these`

@export Is my injury or disease a "service injury" or "service disease" under the MRCA (s 27)?
GIVEN `it began before 1 July 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you sustained the injury or contracted the disease before 1 July 2004 (not encoded)
      `how it happened` IS A `How it happened` @desc Which of the s 27 connections to your defence service applies (the first that fits)
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`Is it a service injury or disease` MEANS
    IF `it began before 1 July 2004`
    THEN `not covered` `a condition sustained or contracted before 1 July 2004 is governed by the transitional provisions, the DRCA or the VEA, which are not encoded`
    ELSE `answered` (NOT (`how it happened` EQUALS `none of these`))

-- s 6(1A): "defence service" is warlike, non-warlike, British nuclear test defence, hazardous or peacetime service (the
-- Defence Minister determines which service is warlike or non-warlike). s 335(1), (2): for a claim relating to warlike,
-- non-warlike, British nuclear test defence or hazardous service, the Commission must find for the claimant unless
-- "satisfied, beyond reasonable doubt, that there is no sufficient ground" -- that is, if the material "does not raise a
-- reasonable hypothesis connecting the injury, disease or death with the circumstances of the particular service". (3):
-- otherwise, including peacetime service, "to his, her or its reasonable satisfaction". (4): not where a s 27A
-- presumption is relied on.
DECLARE `Kind of service` IS ONE OF
    `warlike service`
    `non-warlike service, including peacekeeping`
    `British nuclear test defence service`
    `hazardous service`
    `peacetime service`

DECLARE `Standard of proof` IS ONE OF
    `the reasonable hypothesis standard: the Commission must accept the connection unless satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that there is no sufficient ground (s 335(1), (2))`
    `the reasonable satisfaction standard: the Commission must be reasonably satisfied of the connection (s 335(3))`

@export What standard of proof applies to my claim that my condition is connected to my service (s 335)?
GIVEN `the kind of service` IS A `Kind of service` @desc The kind of defence service your claim relates to (the Defence Minister's determinations say which service is warlike or non-warlike)
GIVETH A `Standard of proof`
`Which standard of proof applies` MEANS
    IF `the kind of service` EQUALS `peacetime service`
    THEN `the reasonable satisfaction standard: the Commission must be reasonably satisfied of the connection (s 335(3))`
    ELSE `the reasonable hypothesis standard: the Commission must accept the connection unless satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that there is no sufficient ground (s 335(1), (2))`

§§ `ss 23, 32 to 36, 319 -- must the Commission accept liability`

-- s 23(1): "The Commission must accept liability for an injury sustained, or a disease contracted, by a person if: (a) the
-- person's injury or disease is a service injury or disease under section 27; and (b) the Commission is not prevented from
-- accepting liability for the injury or disease by Part 4; and (c) a claim for acceptance of liability ... has been made
-- under section 319."
-- Part 4: s 32(1): not if it "resulted from the person's serious default or wilful act while a member", arose from "a
-- serious breach of discipline", or "was intentionally self-inflicted", "except if the injury or disease results in serious
-- and permanent impairment"; (2): being under the influence of alcohol or a drug not lawfully taken counts as serious
-- default. s 33(1): not if it "resulted from: (a) reasonable and appropriate counselling in relation to the person's
-- performance as a member; or (b) a failure to obtain a promotion, transfer or benefit". s 34: not if the person "made a
-- wilful and false representation ... that he or she did not suffer, or had not previously suffered, from that injury or
-- disease". s 35: for peacetime service, not if it resulted from an accident on a journey after a substantial delay, by a
-- route not reasonably direct, or after a substantial interruption, unless for a reason connected with duty or the risk
-- was not substantially changed or increased. s 36: not if related to service only because of tobacco use after 31
-- December 1997 (or increased use, for one who used tobacco before 1 January 1998).
DECLARE `Liability` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Commission must accept liability (s 23(1))`
    `no: it is not a service injury or disease (s 27)`
    `no: no claim for acceptance of liability has been made under s 319 (s 23(1)(c))`
    `no: excluded as the result of my serious default, wilful act, serious breach of discipline or self-infliction, without serious and permanent impairment (s 32)`
    `no: excluded as the result of reasonable and appropriate counselling about my performance, or a failure to get a promotion, transfer or benefit (s 33)`
    `no: excluded because I wilfully and falsely said I did not have, or had not had, the condition (s 34)`
    `no: excluded as a peacetime journey accident after a substantial delay, an indirect route or a substantial interruption (s 35)`
    `no: excluded as related to service only through my tobacco use after 1997 (s 36)`

@export Must the Commission accept liability for my injury or disease (ss 23, 32 to 36)?
GIVEN `it is a service injury or disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury or disease is a service injury or disease under s 27 (see that question)
      `I have claimed acceptance of liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a claim for acceptance of liability has been made to the Commission in writing under s 319
      `it came from my serious default, wilful act, serious breach of discipline or self-infliction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it resulted from your serious default or wilful act (including being under the influence of alcohol or a drug not lawfully taken), a serious breach of discipline, or was intentionally self-inflicted, while a member
      `it has caused serious and permanent impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has resulted in serious and permanent impairment
      `it came from reasonable counselling or a missed promotion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it resulted from reasonable and appropriate counselling about your performance, or from failing to get a promotion, transfer or benefit
      `I falsely said I did not have the condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a wilful and false representation, in connection with your service, that you did not have or had not had this condition
      `a peacetime journey with an unexplained delay, detour or interruption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an accident on a peacetime journey to or from duty: whether you substantially delayed starting it, took a route that was not reasonably direct, or substantially interrupted it, for a reason not connected with your duties and in a way that substantially changed or increased the risk
      `it is related to service only through tobacco use after 1997` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is related to your service only because you used tobacco after 31 December 1997 (or, if you used tobacco before 1998, only because you used more after 1997)
GIVETH A `Liability`
`Must the Commission accept liability` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `it is a service injury or disease`) THEN `no: it is not a service injury or disease (s 27)`
        IF `it came from my serious default, wilful act, serious breach of discipline or self-infliction` AND (NOT `it has caused serious and permanent impairment`)
            THEN `no: excluded as the result of my serious default, wilful act, serious breach of discipline or self-infliction, without serious and permanent impairment (s 32)`
        IF `it came from reasonable counselling or a missed promotion`
            THEN `no: excluded as the result of reasonable and appropriate counselling about my performance, or a failure to get a promotion, transfer or benefit (s 33)`
        IF `I falsely said I did not have the condition`
            THEN `no: excluded because I wilfully and falsely said I did not have, or had not had, the condition (s 34)`
        IF `a peacetime journey with an unexplained delay, detour or interruption`
            THEN `no: excluded as a peacetime journey accident after a substantial delay, an indirect route or a substantial interruption (s 35)`
        IF `it is related to service only through tobacco use after 1997`
            THEN `no: excluded as related to service only through my tobacco use after 1997 (s 36)`
        IF (NOT `I have claimed acceptance of liability`) THEN `no: no claim for acceptance of liability has been made under s 319 (s 23(1)(c))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the Commission must accept liability (s 23(1))`

-- s 319(2): a claim for acceptance of liability for an injury, disease, death or a medical aid "must: (a) be in writing;
-- and (b) be given to the Commission; and (c) satisfy the requirements (if any)" of the regulations or the Commission as
-- to form and content. (2A): a claim for compensation "must: (a) be in writing and be given to the Commission; or (b) be
-- made orally to the Commission."
DECLARE `What I am claiming` IS ONE OF
    `acceptance of liability for an injury, disease, death or medical aid`
    `compensation for a condition already accepted`

DECLARE `How to claim` IS ONE OF
    `in writing, given to the Commission, in the form and with the content the regulations or the Commission require (s 319(2))`
    `in writing given to the Commission, or orally to the Commission (s 319(2A))`

@export How must I make my claim under the MRCA (s 319)?
GIVEN `what I am claiming` IS A `What I am claiming` @desc Whether you are asking the Commission to accept liability for a condition (or a death or a damaged medical aid), or claiming compensation for a condition it has accepted
GIVETH A `How to claim`
`How must I claim` MEANS
    IF `what I am claiming` EQUALS `acceptance of liability for an injury, disease, death or medical aid`
    THEN `in writing, given to the Commission, in the form and with the content the regulations or the Commission require (s 319(2))`
    ELSE `in writing given to the Commission, or orally to the Commission (s 319(2A))`

§§ `ss 68, 69, 74, 77 to 79 -- permanent impairment` -- arises only if an accepted condition has left an impairment

-- s 68(1): the Commonwealth is liable if the Commission has accepted liability for the condition, and "is satisfied that:
-- (i) as a result of the compensable condition, the person has suffered an impairment; and (ii) the impairment is likely to
-- continue indefinitely; and (iii) the person's compensable condition has stabilised", and a claim has been made. s 69:
-- only if "(a) for an impairment resulting from a single service injury or disease consisting of: (i) hearing loss; or
-- (ii) the loss, or the loss of the use, of a finger or toe; or (iii) the loss of the sense of taste or smell; the
-- impairment ... constitutes at least 5 impairment points; and (b) otherwise ... at least 10 impairment points" (points
-- from more than one condition may be combined: note 1 to s 68(1)). The points come from the Guide (s 67), asked as a
-- figure. s 75: if the conditions have not stabilised but the Commission is satisfied the threshold will be met, interim
-- compensation is payable.
DECLARE `Permanent impairment` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I am entitled to weekly permanent impairment compensation (ss 68, 69), up to the maximum weekly amount, which I may convert in whole or part to a lump sum (s 78)`
    `not yet: my condition has not stabilised; interim compensation is payable if the Commission is satisfied the threshold will be met (s 75)`
    `no: the impairment points are below the threshold (s 69)`
    `no: the Commission is not satisfied that I have an impairment likely to continue indefinitely (s 68(1)(b))`
    `no: the Commission has not accepted liability for the condition, or no claim has been made (s 68(1)(a), (c))`

@export Am I entitled to permanent impairment compensation under the MRCA (ss 68, 69, 75)?
GIVEN `the Commission has accepted liability and I have claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission has accepted liability for the condition and a claim for permanent impairment compensation has been made
      `I have an impairment likely to continue indefinitely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is satisfied you have an impairment from the condition that is likely to continue indefinitely
      `my condition has stabilised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is satisfied that your condition has stabilised
      `the single condition is a hearing loss, a finger or toe, or taste or smell` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the impairment comes from a single condition consisting of hearing loss, the loss or loss of use of a finger or toe, or the loss of taste or smell
      `the impairment points` IS A NUMBER @desc The impairment points under the Guide to Determining Impairment and Compensation (combined across conditions where the Commission combines them)
GIVETH A `Permanent impairment`
`Am I entitled to permanent impairment compensation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Commission has accepted liability and I have claimed`)
            THEN `no: the Commission has not accepted liability for the condition, or no claim has been made (s 68(1)(a), (c))`
        IF (NOT `I have an impairment likely to continue indefinitely`)
            THEN `no: the Commission is not satisfied that I have an impairment likely to continue indefinitely (s 68(1)(b))`
        IF `the impairment points` LESS THAN `the threshold`
            THEN `no: the impairment points are below the threshold (s 69)`
        IF (NOT `my condition has stabilised`)
            THEN `not yet: my condition has not stabilised; interim compensation is payable if the Commission is satisfied the threshold will be met (s 75)`
        OTHERWISE `yes: I am entitled to weekly permanent impairment compensation (ss 68, 69), up to the maximum weekly amount, which I may convert in whole or part to a lump sum (s 78)`
    WHERE
        `the threshold` MEANS IF `the single condition is a hearing loss, a finger or toe, or taste or smell` THEN 5 ELSE 10

-- s 68(3): the date of entitlement is "the later of: (a) the date on which a claim was made under section 319 for
-- acceptance of liability for the compensable condition; and (b) the date on which" the impairment became likely to
-- continue indefinitely and the condition stabilised, "as estimated by a medical practitioner". s 77(1): weekly
-- compensation is payable from "(a) if the date ... is the date mentioned in paragraph 68(3)(a)--that date; or (b) if ...
-- the date mentioned in paragraph 68(3)(b)--the first day of the calendar month during which that date occurs."
@export From what day is my weekly permanent impairment compensation payable (ss 68(3), 77(1))?
GIVEN `the day I claimed acceptance of liability` IS A DATE @desc The day your claim for acceptance of liability for the condition was made
      `the day my doctor estimates it stabilised and became indefinite` IS A DATE @desc The day a medical practitioner who examined you estimates your condition stabilised and the impairment became likely to continue indefinitely
GIVETH A DATE
`From when is permanent impairment compensation payable` MEANS
    IF `the day I claimed acceptance of liability` AT LEAST `the day my doctor estimates it stabilised and became indefinite`
    THEN `the day I claimed acceptance of liability`
    ELSE Date 1 (DATE_MONTH `the day my doctor estimates it stabilised and became indefinite`) (DATE_YEAR `the day my doctor estimates it stabilised and became indefinite`)

-- s 74(1): "The maximum weekly amount of compensation payable to a person under this Part ... is $233.07", indexed under s
-- 404 (an input). s 78(1): a person given notice of a weekly amount may choose "(a) to convert 100% of the convertible
-- amount to a lump sum; or (b) if the convertible amount is at least 10%, but not more than 20%, of the maximum weekly
-- amount ...--to convert 50% ...; or (c) if the convertible amount is more than 20% of the maximum weekly amount ...--to
-- convert 25%, 50% or 75%". (2): the choice cannot be changed. The amount of the lump sum is by a formula lost from the
-- deposit and the Australian Government Actuary's advice (s 78(5)).
@export What share of my weekly permanent impairment compensation may I convert to a lump sum (s 78(1))?
GIVEN `my weekly amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly amount of permanent impairment compensation in the Commission's s 76 notice, in dollars
      `the maximum weekly amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 74 maximum weekly amount in force, in dollars ($233.07 in the Act, indexed under s 404)
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`What share may I convert to a lump sum` MEANS
    IF `the ratio` GREATER THAN 0.2
    THEN LIST 25, 50, 75, 100
    ELSE IF `the ratio` AT LEAST 0.1
         THEN LIST 50, 100
         ELSE LIST 100
    WHERE
        `the ratio` MEANS `my weekly amount` DIVIDED BY `the maximum weekly amount`

-- s 78(3): "The choice must be made in writing and must be given to the Commission within 6 months after the date on
-- which the person received the notice"; (4): the Commission may extend it for special circumstances. s 79(1): "The lump
-- sum is payable to the person within 30 days after the date on which the Commission became aware of the choice"; (2):
-- interest after that.
@export By what day must I choose whether to take a lump sum (s 78(3))?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the Commission's s 76 notice of your weekly amount
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I choose a lump sum` MEANS `add months` `the day I received the notice` 6

@export By what day must my lump sum be paid, before interest runs (s 79)?
GIVEN `the day the Commission became aware of my choice` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commission became aware of your written choice to take a lump sum
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my lump sum be paid` MEANS `the day the Commission became aware of my choice` PLUS 30

§§ `ss 118 to 122, 129, 131 -- incapacity compensation for a former member` -- arises only if a former member cannot work, or work as before

-- s 118(1): the Commonwealth is liable for a week if the person "is a former member", the Commission has accepted
-- liability for a service injury or disease that "results in the person's incapacity for work for the week", and a claim
-- has been made; (2)(a): if the person has chosen the Special Rate Disability Pension, Part 6 applies instead (not
-- encoded). s 129(2): "a week is a maximum rate week" if the incapacity prevents working normal weekly hours, or at the
-- pre-incapacity level, and "the total number of hours in that week, and in all previous maximum rate weeks ..., during
-- which the incapacity has prevented the person from so working, does not exceed 45 times the person's normal weekly
-- hours". s 131(2): after that, the "adjustment percentage" is 75% not working; 80% working 25% or less of normal weekly
-- hours; 85% over 25% to 50%; 90% over 50% to 75%; 95% over 75% but under 100%; 100% at 100% or more. The amounts are by
-- formulas lost from the deposit. s 120: none at pension age or older, except (s 121) for a condition sustained at or
-- after the age 2 years before pension age, "for a maximum of 104 weeks". s 122: none for a week of imprisonment for an
-- offence.
GIVEN `the hours I worked this week` IS A NUMBER
      `my normal weekly hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 131 adjustment percentage` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the hours I worked this week` AT MOST 0 THEN 75
        IF `the share` AT MOST 0.25 THEN 80
        IF `the share` AT MOST 0.5 THEN 85
        IF `the share` AT MOST 0.75 THEN 90
        IF `the share` LESS THAN 1 THEN 95
        OTHERWISE 100
    WHERE
        `the share` MEANS `the hours I worked this week` DIVIDED BY `my normal weekly hours`

DECLARE `Incapacity compensation` IS ONE OF
    `a maximum rate week: compensation on my full normal earnings less my actual earnings (s 129)`
    `a reduced rate week: compensation on this adjustment percentage of my normal earnings less my actual earnings (s 131)` HAS `adjustment percentage` IS A NUMBER
    `the Special Rate Disability Pension I chose, worked out under Part 6 (s 118(2)(a)), which is not encoded`
    `none: I am pension age or older (s 120)`
    `none: the 104 weeks for a condition sustained within 2 years before pension age are used up (s 121)`
    `none: I am imprisoned for an offence (s 122)`
    `none: I am incapacitated for work this week by no accepted service condition, or am still a member (s 118(1))`

@export As a former ADF member unable to work, which rate of incapacity compensation applies to me this week (ss 118 to 122, 129, 131)?
GIVEN `I am a former member incapacitated by an accepted condition this week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have left the ADF and an accepted service injury or disease stops you working your normal weekly hours, or at your former level, this week (and you have claimed)
      `I chose the Special Rate Disability Pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have chosen to receive the Special Rate Disability Pension under Part 6
      `my normal weekly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc Your normal weekly hours (as s 132 works them out)
      `the hours lost to incapacity to the end of this week` IS A NUMBER @desc The total hours, in this week and all earlier maximum rate weeks, that the incapacity has stopped you working (or working at your former level)
      `the hours I worked this week` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours you worked this week (0 if none)
      `I am pension age or older` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have reached pension age under the Social Security Act 1991
      `the condition began within 2 years before pension age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you sustained the injury or contracted the disease at or after the age 2 years before your pension age
      `the weeks of incapacity already compensated` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of incapacity have already been compensated (counted only for a condition within 2 years before pension age)
      `I am imprisoned for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in prison this week in connection with your conviction of an offence
GIVETH AN `Incapacity compensation`
`Which incapacity rate applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `I am a former member incapacitated by an accepted condition this week`)
            THEN `none: I am incapacitated for work this week by no accepted service condition, or am still a member (s 118(1))`
        IF `I chose the Special Rate Disability Pension` THEN `the Special Rate Disability Pension I chose, worked out under Part 6 (s 118(2)(a)), which is not encoded`
        IF `I am imprisoned for an offence` THEN `none: I am imprisoned for an offence (s 122)`
        IF `the condition began within 2 years before pension age` AND `the weeks of incapacity already compensated` AT LEAST 104
            THEN `none: the 104 weeks for a condition sustained within 2 years before pension age are used up (s 121)`
        IF `I am pension age or older` AND (NOT `the condition began within 2 years before pension age`)
            THEN `none: I am pension age or older (s 120)`
        IF `the hours lost to incapacity to the end of this week` AT MOST (45 TIMES `my normal weekly hours`)
            THEN `a maximum rate week: compensation on my full normal earnings less my actual earnings (s 129)`
        OTHERWISE `a reduced rate week: compensation on this adjustment percentage of my normal earnings less my actual earnings (s 131)` (`the s 131 adjustment percentage` `the hours I worked this week` `my normal weekly hours`)

§§ `ss 345, 352A, 352B, 354 -- review`

-- s 346(5): the notice of an original determination says the claimant "may, if dissatisfied with the original
-- determination, make an application to the Board under Part 4". s 352A: "The claimant may make an application to the
-- Board for review of an original determination." s 352B(1): it "must: (a) be in writing; and (b) be given to the Board
-- within 12 months after the day on which notice of the original determination was given". s 345(1): a "reviewable
-- determination" is one revoking, confirming or varying an original determination on reconsideration (s 350(2)), or the
-- Board's determination on review. s 354(1): "An application may be made to the Tribunal for review of a reviewable
-- determination."
@export By what day must I apply to the Veterans' Review Board for review of the Commission's determination (s 352B)?
GIVEN `the day I was given notice of the determination` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given notice of the Commission's original determination
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply to the Board` MEANS `add months` `the day I was given notice of the determination` 12

DECLARE `Where I take the determination` IS ONE OF
    `the Veterans' Review Board first: apply in writing within 12 months of the notice (ss 352A, 352B); the Tribunal reviews only a reviewable determination (s 354)`
    `I may apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal for review of the reviewable determination (s 354(1))`

@export Can I take the Commission's determination straight to the Administrative Review Tribunal (ss 345, 352A, 354)?
GIVEN `the Board has reviewed it, or it was reconsidered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Veterans' Review Board has made a determination on review of it, or the Commission has made a determination on reconsideration revoking, confirming or varying it
GIVETH A `Where I take the determination`
`Can I go straight to the Tribunal` MEANS
    IF `the Board has reviewed it, or it was reconsidered`
    THEN `I may apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal for review of the reviewable determination (s 354(1))`
    ELSE `the Veterans' Review Board first: apply in writing within 12 months of the notice (ss 352A, 352B); the Tribunal reviews only a reviewable determination (s 354)`
